 <p>I'll Ask For It ("the Site," "we," "us," or "our") is a personal opinion website operated by an individual at <strong>illaskforit.com</strong>. This Privacy Policy explains what information — if any — is collected when you visit the Site, how it is used, and what rights you have regarding that information.</p>
 <p>By accessing or using the Site, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.</p>
 <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
-<p><strong>No personally identifiable information is collected directly by this Site.</strong> There are no account registrations, contact forms, newsletter signups, or comment systems. You can read every page on this Site without providing any information about yourself.</p>
-<p>However, certain information may be collected automatically through third-party services used to deliver this Site:</p>
+<p><strong>This Site does not collect personal information beyond what you choose to give us.</strong> There are no account registrations, contact forms, or comment systems. You can read every page on this Site without providing any information about yourself.</p>
+<p><strong>Newsletter Signup:</strong> If you choose to subscribe to our email list, we collect the email address you provide. That information is processed by Brevo (formerly Sendinblue), our email service provider, and is used only to send you the newsletter you signed up for. We do not sell, rent, or share your email address with any other third party. Every email includes an unsubscribe link, and you can ask us to delete your information at any time by contacting us at the address on our <a href="about.html">About page</a>. See <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brevo's Privacy Policy</a> for details on how they handle this data.</p>
+<p>If you email us directly, we will have your email address and whatever you send us. We use that only to reply to you.</p>
+<p>Beyond the newsletter signup and direct email, certain information may be collected automatically through third-party services used to deliver this Site:</p>
 <p><strong>GitHub Pages (Hosting):</strong> This Site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service provided by GitHub, Inc. GitHub may collect server log data including your IP address, browser type, referring/exit pages, and timestamps when you access the Site. This data is subject to <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
 <p><strong>Google Fonts:</strong> This Site loads fonts from Google Fonts, a service provided by Google LLC. When fonts are loaded, your browser makes a request to Google's servers, which may log your IP address and browser information. This data is subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
 <h3>2. Cookies and Tracking</h3>
 <p>This Site uses Google Analytics (GA4), a web analytics service provided by Google LLC, to help us understand how visitors use the Site, such as pages viewed and approximate location derived from IP address. Google Analytics uses cookies to collect this information. We do not use tracking pixels, advertising networks, or any other behavioral tracking technology beyond Google Analytics. You can opt out using the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>
 <p>Third-party services used for hosting, font delivery, and analytics (GitHub Pages, Google Fonts, and Google Analytics) may set their own cookies or employ their own tracking mechanisms. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of those services directly, including <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
 <h3>3. How Information Is Used</h3>
-<p>We do not collect or process personal data. Any data collected by third-party infrastructure providers (GitHub, Google) is used by those providers in accordance with their own privacy policies and is not accessible to or controlled by us.</p>
+<p>Your email address is used only to send you the newsletter you signed up for, or to reply to you if you email us directly. We do not use it for any other purpose. Any data collected by third-party infrastructure providers (GitHub, Google) is used by those providers in accordance with their own privacy policies and is not accessible to or controlled by us.</p>
 <h3>4. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h3>
-<p>We do not sell, rent, trade, or otherwise transfer any information about visitors to third parties. We have no data to share. If we were ever compelled by law to disclose user information, we would have nothing to provide — because we do not collect it.</p>
+<p>We do not sell, rent, trade, or otherwise transfer any information about visitors to third parties. Your email address is shared only with Brevo, the third-party service that delivers our newsletter on our behalf. If we were ever compelled by law to disclose user information, we would provide only what we actually have — which, beyond the newsletter list, is very little.</p>
 <h3>5. Children's Privacy</h3>
 <p>This Site is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.</p>
 <h3>6. External Links</h3>
 <p>The Site may contain links to external websites. This Privacy Policy applies only to <strong>illaskforit.com</strong>. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of any external sites. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of any site you visit. Some links on this Site are affiliate links, including links through the Amazon Associates Program. If you click one of these links and make a purchase, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. See our <a href="affiliate-disclosure.html">Affiliate Disclosure</a> for details.</p>
 <h3>7. Data Security</h3>
-<p>Since we do not collect personal data, there is no personal data for us to secure. The Site is served over HTTPS to protect data in transit between your browser and our hosting provider. No sensitive information is transmitted through this Site.</p>
+<p>We collect very little personal data, and what we do collect (your email address, if you subscribe) is held by Brevo, a reputable email service provider, rather than on our own servers. The Site is served over HTTPS to protect data in transit between your browser and our hosting provider.</p>
 <h3>8. Your Rights</h3>
-<p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights regarding personal data under laws such as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), or other applicable privacy laws. Because we do not collect personal data, there is generally no data to access, correct, delete, or port. If you have questions or concerns about your rights, you may contact us at the address below.</p>
