-</head><body><nav><a href="index.html" class="nav-wordmark">I'll Ask <em>For It</em></a><ul class="nav-links" id="navLinks"><li><a href="category-opinions.html">One Man's Opinion</a></li><li><a href="category-indy.html">Circle City</a></li><li><a href="category-food.html">Food &amp; Drink</a></li><li><a href="category-music.html">Music</a></li><li><a href="category-sports.html">Sports</a></li><li><a href="category-travel.html">Worth the Trip</a></li><li><a href="category-nostalgia.html">Nostalgia</a></li><li><a href="things-you-didnt-know-you-needed.html">Cool Shit</a></li><li><a href="deeper-dive.html">Deeper Dive</a></li><li><a href="about.html" class="nav-cta">About</a></li></ul><button class="hamburger" onclick="document.getElementById('navLinks').classList.toggle('open')" aria-label="Menu"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></nav><div class="ticker"><div class="ticker-inner"><span>One Man's Opinion</span><span>Indianapolis Institutions</span><span>Food &amp; Drink</span><span>Music</span><span>Sports</span><span>Worth the Trip</span><span>Nostalgia</span><span>Hold My Beer</span><span>One Man's Opinion</span><span>Indianapolis Institutions</span><span>Food &amp; Drink</span><span>Music</span><span>Sports</span><span>Worth the Trip</span><span>Nostalgia</span><span>Hold My Beer</span></div></div><div class="champ-banner"><p>🏈 <em>2026 CFP National Champions · 16-0 · Indiana Hoosiers</em> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Nothing But Time and Opinions &nbsp;·&nbsp; <em>I'll Ask For It</em></p></div><section class="list-hero"><div class="list-hero-inner"><p class="list-hero-label">Indy Sports · Top 10 List</p><h1 class="list-hero-title">Top 10 Indy Sports Moments</h1><p class="list-hero-subtitle">From Reggie to the Colts to 16-0. The moments that made Indianapolis a real sports city.</p><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;margin-top:1.2rem"><img src="images/sean-matthews-avatar.jpg" alt="Sean Matthews" style="width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;object-fit:cover;border:2px solid #cc0000;flex-shrink:0"><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgba(245,245,245,0.6);margin:0">Words by Sean Matthews · Indy Sports · Top 10 List</p></div></div></section><section class="list-body"><div class="list-body-inner"><a href="index.html" class="back-link">← Back to Home</a><p class="list-intro">Indianapolis has always been a sports city. People from the coasts just didn't notice until it was impossible to ignore. These are the ten moments that made it undeniable. Ranked, not just remembered — somebody has to say which one was first.</p><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">10</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Indiana Hoosiers Go 16-0 — 2025-26 CFP National Champions</div><div class="list-item-desc">The program that had been building finally arrived. Sixteen wins, zero losses, and a national championship that nobody outside Indiana could argue with. The city celebrated like it had been waiting forty years. It had.</div><span class="list-item-note">We Are IU</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">09</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Peyton Manning's Super Bowl XLI Win — February 2007</div><div class="list-item-desc">The MVP performance in the rain in Miami. The monkey off the back. Indianapolis watched the Colts beat the Bears 29-17 and then poured into the streets. The quarterback the city loved finally had the ring.</div><span class="list-item-note">The Ring</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">08</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Reggie Miller's 8 Points in 8.9 Seconds — May 7, 1995</div><div class="list-item-desc">The Knicks led by six with under ten seconds. Then: three. Then: a foul drawn. Then: two free throws. Then: a stolen inbound. Then: a three. Eight points in 8.9 seconds. Spike Lee just watched.</div><span class="list-item-note">Impossible</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">07</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">The Colts' Perfect Regular Season — 2009</div><div class="list-item-desc">14-0 before Bill Polian rested his starters. The city had never seen a team that dominant. Manning to Harrison. Marvin Harrison catching everything. A team that made you watch every snap.</div><span class="list-item-note">14-0</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">06</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Pacers Push the Celtics to the Brink — 1991</div><div class="list-item-desc">A young, unheralded Pacers team took the heavily favored Celtics to five games before Boston survived. The Reggie era was beginning. The city was starting to understand what it had. Market Square Arena was never louder.</div><span class="list-item-note">Almost</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">05</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Larry Bird Leads Indiana State to the NCAA Final — 1979</div><div class="list-item-desc">The undefeated regular season. The run to the championship game. Magic vs. Bird in the final, the game that saved college basketball and launched two careers that would define the next decade.</div><span class="list-item-note">French Lick to Final</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">04</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Tony George Launches the IRL — 1996</div><div class="list-item-desc">The split was messy. The politics were real. But Tony George's decision to create the Indy Racing League kept open-wheel racing American and kept the 500 its own thing. History will argue about this one.</div><span class="list-item-note">Consequential</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">03</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">The Indianapolis 500 Returns After WWII — 1946</div><div class="list-item-desc">The first race back after the war. One hundred thousand people showed up to watch thirty-three cars take the green flag. The sound of engines after four years of silence. Some moments earn their mythology.</div><span class="list-item-note">Historic</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">02</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Reggie Miller's Final Game at Conseco Fieldhouse — April 30, 2005</div><div class="list-item-desc">He played 18 seasons. Scored 25,279 points. Never won a ring. And when he walked off the court for the last time, the entire building stood for ten minutes and wouldn't stop. Pacers fans knew what they had.</div><span class="list-item-note">Goodbye Reggie</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">01</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Conseco Fieldhouse Opens — 1999</div><div class="list-item-desc">When the arena opened, it was immediately called the best in the NBA. The brick exterior. The sky boxes that look like a high school gym scaled up. The building that proved Indianapolis could have something world-class.</div><span class="list-item-note">Home</span></div></div></div></section><footer><div class="footer-inner"><div class="footer-brand"><div class="wordmark">I'll Ask <em>For It</em></div><div class="tagline">Nothing But Time and Opinions</div></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>Topics</h4><ul><li><a href="category-opinions.html">One Man's Opinion</a></li><li><a href="category-indy.html">Circle City</a></li><li><a href="category-food.html">Food &amp; Drink</a></li><li><a href="category-music.html">Music</a></li><li><a href="category-sports.html">Sports</a></li><li><a href="category-travel.html">Worth the Trip</a></li><li><a href="category-nostalgia.html">Nostalgia</a></li><li><a href="hold-my-beer.html">Hold My Beer</a></li></ul></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>Top 10 Lists</h4><ul><li><a href="top10-restaurants.html">Restaurants</a></li><li><a href="top10-athletes.html">Athletes</a></li><li><a href="top10-things-to-do.html">Things To Do</a></li><li><a href="top10-trails.html">Trails</a></li><li><a href="top10-indy-sports.html">Indy Sports Moments</a></li><li><a href="top10-albums.html">Albums</a></li></ul></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>The Site</h4><ul><li><a href="about.html">About</a></li><li><a href="archive.html">Full Archive</a></li><li><a href="about.html#contact">Contact</a></li></ul></div></div><div class="footer-bottom"><p class="footer-copy">© 2026 <em>I'll Ask For It</em> · Nothing But Time and Opinions</p><div class="footer-legal">
