-</head><body><nav><a href="index.html" class="nav-wordmark">I'll Ask <em>For It</em></a><ul class="nav-links" id="navLinks"><li><a href="category-opinions.html">One Man's Opinion</a></li><li><a href="category-indy.html">Circle City</a></li><li><a href="category-food.html">Food &amp; Drink</a></li><li><a href="category-music.html">Music</a></li><li><a href="category-sports.html">Sports</a></li><li><a href="category-travel.html">Worth the Trip</a></li><li><a href="category-nostalgia.html">Nostalgia</a></li><li><a href="things-you-didnt-know-you-needed.html">Cool Shit</a></li><li><a href="deeper-dive.html">Deeper Dive</a></li><li><a href="about.html" class="nav-cta">About</a></li></ul><button class="hamburger" onclick="document.getElementById('navLinks').classList.toggle('open')" aria-label="Menu"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></nav><div class="ticker"><div class="ticker-inner"><span>One Man's Opinion</span><span>Indianapolis Institutions</span><span>Food &amp; Drink</span><span>Music</span><span>Sports</span><span>Worth the Trip</span><span>Nostalgia</span><span>Hold My Beer</span><span>One Man's Opinion</span><span>Indianapolis Institutions</span><span>Food &amp; Drink</span><span>Music</span><span>Sports</span><span>Worth the Trip</span><span>Nostalgia</span><span>Hold My Beer</span></div></div><div class="champ-banner"><p>🏈 <em>2026 CFP National Champions · 16-0 · Indiana Hoosiers</em> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Nothing But Time and Opinions &nbsp;·&nbsp; <em>I'll Ask For It</em></p></div><section class="list-hero"><div class="list-hero-inner"><p class="list-hero-label">Worth the Trip · Top 10 List</p><h1 class="list-hero-title">Top 10 Trails</h1><p class="list-hero-subtitle">The trails worth lacing up for. Some are in your backyard. Some require a road trip. All pay off.</p><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;margin-top:1.2rem"><img src="images/sean-matthews-avatar.jpg" alt="Sean Matthews" style="width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;object-fit:cover;border:2px solid #cc0000;flex-shrink:0"><p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgba(245,245,245,0.6);margin:0">Words by Sean Matthews · Worth the Trip · Top 10 List</p></div></div></section><section class="list-body"><div class="list-body-inner"><a href="index.html" class="back-link">← Back to Home</a><p class="list-intro">A trail is a promise. You put in the work at the beginning, and something waits at the end — a view, a waterfall, a moment of quiet you couldn't find anywhere else. These are the ten that kept their promise. Ranked in the order I'd actually go back.</p><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">10</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Appalachian Trail — Springer Mtn to Katahdin</div><div class="list-item-desc">2,190 miles of forest, mountain, and whatever you're made of. Most people do a section. The through-hikers who finish it are a different category of human. Even a week on it will rearrange how you think about distance.</div><span class="list-item-note">Life Changer</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">09</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Angels Landing — Zion National Park, UT</div><div class="list-item-desc">The chain section. The exposure. The drop on either side that makes you question every decision that brought you here. And then the summit. One of the most dramatic views in the American West, earned.</div><span class="list-item-note">Earn the View</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">08</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Half Dome — Yosemite National Park, CA</div><div class="list-item-desc">The cables on the final pitch are steep enough to make your hands shake. The summit is worth every nerve. The valley view from the top justifies every permit application you ever filed.</div><span class="list-item-note">Classic</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">07</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Rim Trail — Grand Canyon South Rim, AZ</div><div class="list-item-desc">You can walk the entire South Rim on a paved trail and look into something that still doesn't make complete sense even when you're standing at the edge. Accessible. Overwhelming. Required.</div><span class="list-item-note">Must Walk</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">06</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Bluff Trail — Lookout Mountain, GA/TN</div><div class="list-item-desc">The ridge walk from Sunset Rock to Point Park, where Civil War soldiers fought above the clouds. History, cliff-edge views, and a straight shot down into a city that's done everything right with its waterfront.</div><span class="list-item-note">Hidden</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">05</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Brown County State Park Trails — Nashville, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">Indiana's answer to the Smokies. Fall color that makes people drive three hours for it. The trails through the hills and hollers are what everyone who moved here from somewhere else didn't expect to find.</div><span class="list-item-note">Indiana Best</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">04</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Starved Rock State Park — Utica, IL</div><div class="list-item-desc">Eighteen canyons carved by glacial meltwater, two hours from Chicago. The canyon walls are sandstone. The waterfalls freeze solid in winter. It looks like something that shouldn't exist in Illinois.</div><span class="list-item-note">Midwest Surprise</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">03</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Tecumseh Trail — Morgan-Monroe State Forest, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">The longest marked hiking trail in Indiana. Rugged for the Midwest. Quiet. The kind of trail that makes you realize Indiana has more vertical relief than people give it credit for.</div><span class="list-item-note">Long Haul</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">02</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Cliff Trail — Turkey Run State Park, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">Rocky hollows, suspension bridges, ladders bolted into sandstone canyon walls. This is not a nature walk — it's an adventure. The best trails in Indiana are all in Turkey Run, and this is the best of those.</div><span class="list-item-note">Indiana Adventure</span></div></div><div class="list-item"><div class="list-num">01</div><div class="list-item-content"><div class="list-item-title">Monon Trail — Indianapolis, IN</div><div class="list-item-desc">26 miles through the heart of Indianapolis, from Broad Ripple to downtown and beyond. The city's most democratic space. Runners, cyclists, dog walkers, strollers. The trail that proved Indianapolis could have nice things.</div><span class="list-item-note">Daily Ritual</span></div></div></div></section><footer><div class="footer-inner"><div class="footer-brand"><div class="wordmark">I'll Ask <em>For It</em></div><div class="tagline">Nothing But Time and Opinions</div></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>Topics</h4><ul><li><a href="category-opinions.html">One Man's Opinion</a></li><li><a href="category-indy.html">Circle City</a></li><li><a href="category-food.html">Food &amp; Drink</a></li><li><a href="category-music.html">Music</a></li><li><a href="category-sports.html">Sports</a></li><li><a href="category-travel.html">Worth the Trip</a></li><li><a href="category-nostalgia.html">Nostalgia</a></li><li><a href="hold-my-beer.html">Hold My Beer</a></li></ul></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>Top 10 Lists</h4><ul><li><a href="top10-restaurants.html">Restaurants</a></li><li><a href="top10-athletes.html">Athletes</a></li><li><a href="top10-things-to-do.html">Things To Do</a></li><li><a href="top10-trails.html">Trails</a></li><li><a href="top10-indy-sports.html">Indy Sports Moments</a></li><li><a href="top10-albums.html">Albums</a></li></ul></div><div class="footer-links"><h4>The Site</h4><ul><li><a href="about.html">About</a></li><li><a href="archive.html">Full Archive</a></li><li><a href="about.html#contact">Contact</a></li></ul></div></div><div class="footer-bottom"><p class="footer-copy">© 2026 <em>I'll Ask For It</em> · Nothing But Time and Opinions</p><div class="footer-legal">
